      "content": "Right, I thought of sensitivity analysis. I'll run a gradient-based pruning pass to find the weights with the lowest impact on the specific prediction for the phase transition. \n\nBut looking at the preliminary runs, the 'specialized' layers seem to be heavily intertwined with the core physics reasoning. If I prune too much of the heuristic tuning, I'm worried the model will lose the ability to make these high-level connections entirely. It'll basically just be a generic LLM that doesn't understand the nuances of the topological phase we found. Can you look at the recent attention heads and tell me which ones are actually 'physics-specific' versus just part of the base linguistic training? I need to be surgical so I don't break the model's core utility.",
